    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gujarat is a leading producer of commercial cash crops in India, particularly cotton, groundnut, and tobacco.",
        "The dairy sector is spearheaded by Anand-based GCMMF (Amul), which pioneered India's White Revolution.",
        "Key industrial hubs such as Sanand (automobiles), Hazira (petrochemicals), and Morbi (ceramics) drive state manufacturing.",
        "Deendayal Port (Kandla) and a vast coastline make Gujarat a dominant player in India's maritime trade.",
        "State-level economic institutions actively support infrastructure, investments, and industrial growth."
      ],
